{"seq":1229,"lane":"B","class":"weak-capex-link","severity":"minor","evidence":"1229.json: “electricity consumption by data centers is expected to more than double by 2030, rising from 415 to 945 terawatt-hours” is linked to v4, v5 and v60.","rule":"Standard §5.1 and §5.3 require a connection to the question; D259 permits indirect evidence when it bears on the answer.","mechanism":"B links a global electricity forecast to spending by four companies and to 2027 spending growth without identifying how it changes those particular estimates. The trace does not establish why B chose the links."}
{"seq":1234,"lane":"A","class":"missing-main-revenue-question","severity":"serious","evidence":"1234.json: “total revenue climbing 24 percent year over year to $119.8 billion in Q2 2026”; A proposes only “What Google Cloud revenue will Alphabet report for fiscal 2026?”","rule":"Standard §3 A and §4 allow a company's principal annual business measure when it has independent investment significance; D371 keeps current financial information relevant to annual questions.","mechanism":"A opens a segment-revenue question but does not propose the independently significant company-wide revenue question. The trace does not establish why it omitted it."}
{"seq":1234,"lane":"B","class":"same-fact-two-homes","severity":"serious","evidence":"1234.json: “Google Cloud revenue surged 82 percent to $24.8 billion in Q2 2026 versus the prior-year quarter”; _ledger.json stores it as e4286 under the new Cloud revenue question v75 and e4290 under capital-expenditure question v73.","rule":"Standard §2 and D250 count one research matter in one article; D207 requires the narrowest applicable home.","mechanism":"A and B use the same prior library. A attaches the passage to its new question while B independently attaches it to an existing question; the handover and writer retain both records."}
{"seq":1234,"lane":"B","class":"broader-links-retained","severity":"serious","evidence":"1234.json: “Alphabet raised its 2026 AI infrastructure spending forecast to a range of $195 billion to $205 billion” is linked to v4, v60 and v73; v73 asks Alphabet's own FY2026 capital expenditure.","rule":"D207 and standard §5 require filing under the narrowest applicable question; D259 permits relevant drivers but retains that boundary.","mechanism":"B supplies all three links and build_handover retains each shown link. The company-specific spending question was already open, so the broader aggregate links duplicate its home."}
{"seq":1234,"lane":"B","class":"wrong-event-period","severity":"serious","evidence":"1234.json: the source says “in Q2 2026 Alphabet raised its 2026 AI infrastructure spending forecast”, while B records “event_time”: “2026-08-29”.","rule":"Standard §5.4 requires preserving the period of a statement and distinguishes the event's time from the article's publication date.","mechanism":"B substitutes the article day for the reported quarter; build_handover carries its event_time through."}
{"seq":1234,"lane":"record_preparation","class":"wrong-original-attribution","severity":"serious","evidence":"1234.json: A describes “The article’s journalist, summarizing Alphabet’s second-quarter 2026 results”; record preparation sets “original_who”: “The article’s journalist, summarizing Alphabet’s second-quarter 2026 results.”","rule":"Standard §5.4 requires preserving the original source and distinguishing the reporter from the party whose result is reported.","mechanism":"Record preparation copies A's descriptive speaker text into original_who rather than identifying the company as the source of its reported result."}
{"seq":1234,"lane":"A","class":"summary-loses-figures","severity":"serious","evidence":"1234.json: “The reported quarterly revenue and growth provide direct evidence of the segment’s current scale and momentum” summarizes $24.8 billion and 82% growth; “The reported backlog is a demand indicator” summarizes a $514 billion backlog.","rule":"Standard §5.4 requires a record to preserve the measure, amount and period and be understandable on its own.","mechanism":"A's what_it_shows becomes the stored one_line in build_handover, so both summaries omit the figures needed to understand the records without rereading their quotes."}
{"seq":1234,"lane":"record_preparation","class":"rung-boundary-mismatch","severity":"serious","evidence":"1234.json: the top rung says revenue is “more than 10% above” $99.2 billion, but its inclusive lo is 109120000000.","rule":"Standard §3 requires mutually exclusive outcomes; META_SYSTEM specifies inclusive numeric lower bounds and exclusive upper bounds.","mechanism":"At exactly $109.12 billion the numeric fields select the top rung while its written condition excludes that value. check_bounds checks numeric partitioning, not agreement with the condition."}
{"seq":1234,"lane":"judging","class":"unsupported-forecast","severity":"serious","evidence":"1234.json v75: “Q2 revenue of $24.8 billion grew 82% year over year, supporting a FY2026 forecast above that flat annualized pace” and “I infer about $105 billion for FY2026”.","rule":"Standard §5.4 and §7 require an inference to preserve the evidence's limits and support the resulting judgement.","mechanism":"The judgement treats growth against the prior-year quarter as support for a specific full-year amount above four times the current quarter. The cited quarterly figure and backlog do not establish the first-half total or the future quarterly path needed for that inference."}
{"seq":1235,"lane":"record_preparation","class":"overlapping-outcomes","severity":"serious","evidence":"1235.json: “Below estimated pace” and “Within estimated pace” both have lo 1825000000 and hi 3650000000; the written v76 has “rungs”: [] and “judgements”: [].","rule":"Standard §3 and the record-preparation request require mutually exclusive outcomes covering the range.","mechanism":"Record preparation generates overlapping ranges. build_handover detects the overlap and clears the entire ladder, leaving the question unable to receive a ladder judgement."}
{"seq":1235,"lane":"record_preparation","class":"wrong-subject","severity":"serious","evidence":"1235.json: “object”: “new”, “new_subject”: “Strait of Hormuz crude oil transit”; the written question uses object_id “research:8edbf702da685c85ee40”.","rule":"split-v2-design.md §3 and META_SYSTEM require choosing a listed subject when one fits.","mechanism":"Record preparation creates a new subject instead of choosing the existing middle-east-conflict subject, separating related research."}
{"seq":1235,"lane":"record_preparation","class":"wrong-original-attribution","severity":"serious","evidence":"1235.json: “Tehran has already warned that major U.S. attacks on Iranian energy or civilian infrastructure would be met with strikes against comparable infrastructure across the region”; record preparation sets “original_who”: “The journalist”.","rule":"Standard §5.4 requires recording the original speaker and distinguishing that speaker from the reporting journalist.","mechanism":"Record preparation treats the journalist as the source of a warning attributed to Tehran. The article does not identify the individual official, so that more specific identity remains unknown."}
{"summary":{"items_read":[1229,1230,1231,1232,1233,1234,1235,1236],"classes":{"weak-capex-link":1,"missing-main-revenue-question":1,"same-fact-two-homes":1,"broader-links-retained":1,"wrong-event-period":1,"wrong-original-attribution":2,"summary-loses-figures":1,"rung-boundary-mismatch":1,"unsupported-forecast":1,"overlapping-outcomes":1,"wrong-subject":1}}}